WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:04.400
Madagascar is a big island off the east

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:06.640
coast of Africa, and is one of the

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.040
poorest countries in the world.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:11.280
On average, people there earn just over a

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.760
dollar a day. And right now, there's a

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.640
drought in the south - the worst in 40

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.720
years.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.880
Just look at this satellite image, it

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.360
uses infrared technology to show whether

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.439
vegetation is healthy. Basically, the

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.840
darker the brown, the worse it is. And

00:01:23.439 --> 00:01:27.840
there's a lot of dark brown. Almost

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:32.640
everyone there relies on growing their

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.640
own food, so this drought is devastating.

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:14.400
More than a

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:17.120
million people in southern Madagascar

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.879
are what the U.N. calls, food insecure. That

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.840
means they can't get enough nutritious

00:02:18.879 --> 00:02:24.319
food to eat. And out of those, around 14,000 

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.640
are in what's called ‘phase 5’ - the

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:28.400
catastrophe stage. That's when people

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.879
start dying of starvation or

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:33.599
malnutrition and disease. And that number

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:35.599
is expected to double by October, because

00:02:33.599 --> 00:02:37.360
no one's sure the rain is going to come

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:39.519
and Madagascar is heading into what's

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:42.160
known as lean season. 

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:04.640
So how did Madagascar

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.560
end up here? Well, there are lots of

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.640
reasons. For decades, the governments have

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:10.319
been pretty unstable, and the country

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.040
ranks near the bottom in a lot of

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:15.440
important categories. Whether it's income,

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.440
corruption, or what the World Bank calls

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.519
‘human capital’. Basically, whether a

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.840
country invests in things like education

00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:24.480
and health. That's the baseline.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.599
Then you add COVID-19, the complications

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:29.959
that brings,

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:29.959
and then there's climate change.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:40.000
So we know that greenhouse gas emissions

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.680
are leading to more extreme weather. That

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.319
was one of the big conclusions in a

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:46.799
recent report by the IPCC - the world's

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:48.640
top climate scientists. And when it comes

00:03:46.799 --> 00:03:51.519
to Madagascar, there are really two

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:54.080
things going on. One on land, one at sea.

00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:56.400
Let's start on land. Southern Madagascar

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:58.560
is already pretty dry, but the last six

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:00.560
years have been exceptionally warm. When

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.959
the air is warmer, the molecules move

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:05.760
further apart and the air can hold more

00:04:02.959 --> 00:04:07.840
water vapor, which means it can suck up

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.159
more moisture from the land.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:11.519
So if the land is already dry because of

00:04:10.159 --> 00:04:13.920
a lack of rain,

00:04:11.519 --> 00:04:16.239
warmer air makes it all worse. It's like

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.759
the atmosphere is thirstier.

00:04:16.239 --> 00:04:19.759
Now, what's happening in the sea is that

00:04:17.759 --> 00:04:22.320
global warming is creating pockets of

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:24.400
water that are exceptionally warm.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:27.040
That changes the wind patterns, and leads

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:30.000
to more rain in those areas.

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:10.560
This is what environmentalists mean when

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:14.080
they talk about ‘Climate Justice’.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:16.320
Madagascar produces just 0.01 percent

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:18.960
of all global carbon emissions - but look

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:20.880
what's happening. 

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.960
That issue is going to be

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:48.320
on the table at COP26, the major U.N.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:50.400
climate summit that's happening in

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.919
November. 

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:27.440
Right now in Madagascar, humanitarian

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:29.600
groups are working hard to get food to

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:32.080
the people who need it most. But the

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:34.080
bigger questions aren't going away.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.160
Like how we make sure millions more

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.160
don't starve because of what we're doing

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.680
to the planet.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.680
If you're interested in the debate about

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:44.240
how to protect the environment, check out

